# Chrome/test scratch
.chrome-profile/
/tmp/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor
.DS_Store
*.swp

# NOTE ON THE EXPORTED FRAMES
# assets/frames/*.atlasframe IS committed so the sandbox runs from a fresh
# checkout without needing the datasets mounted (~3.5 MB total).
#
# Those files are derived from KITTI (CC BY-NC-SA) and nuScenes, whose terms
# restrict redistribution. BEFORE PUSHING THIS ANYWHERE PUBLIC, either confirm
# redistribution of derived point clouds is permitted or uncomment the line
# below and rely on tools/export_frames.py to regenerate them locally.
# assets/frames/*.atlasframe

# THE INJECTION TRACES ARE NOT COMMITTED
# atlas/trace_*.pkl and the per-dataset copies are the extracted vehicle point
# clouds ATLAS injects - 159 MB, one file at 97 MiB, near GitHub's per-file
# ceiling. They were never committed in the pipeline repo either. Regenerate
# with atlas/build_nuscenes_assets.py / atlas/build_kitti_assets.py, which need
# the raw dataset archives and OpenPCDet.
trace_*.pkl

# THE OSF k6nf2 RAW CAPTURES ARE NOT COMMITTED
# validation/osf_k6nf2/ ships the analysis scripts and the small real_*.npz
# summaries they produce. The source captures (375 MB of PCAP, 67 MB of
# multimode analysis, from a 2.5 GB archive) come from OSF deposit k6nf2 -
# see validation/osf_k6nf2/README.md for what to download and where to put it.
validation/osf_k6nf2/Moving Target Experiment PCAP file/
validation/osf_k6nf2/Multimode Analysis/
validation/osf_k6nf2/*.pcap
validation/osf_k6nf2/*.zip

# Generated attack data and eval output
eval/output/
eval/*.pkl

# WORKING NOTES ARE LOCAL-ONLY
# docs/ held the long-form notes that used to be inline in the README: how the sandbox
# works, where the constants come from, findings, limitations, data sources. Useful to
# whoever is working on this, not to someone who just wants the attack. README.md and
# the per-directory READMEs are what ship.
docs/

# RESULTS ARE LOCAL-ONLY
# results/ held the paper's reported numbers, the real-world validation writeup, the
# metrics PDF and the BEV figures. Deliberately not published from this repo - the
# results belong with the paper, and this repo is the attack and its harness.
#
# The directory is still on disk and untouched; it is just not tracked. That includes
# rebuttal.md, the OpenReview response, which was never published here (it quotes
# reviewers who did not consent) and was purged from this repo's history rather than
# only deleted at the tip.
results/
